    cml:logicSummary "Classifies the Interpretation Ordinance 1967 as a duty to apply its provisions" ;
    cml:premiseText "(3) The Interpretation Ordinance 1967 of the Australian Capital Territory, as amended and in force from time to time, applies..." ;
    cml:conclusionText "...shall be deemed to have always applied" ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "0.5000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-3-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "3(3) Validation of provisions of Australian Capital Territory Evidence" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The Interpretation Ordinance 1967 of the Australian Capital Territory, as amended and in force from time to time, applies, and shall be deemed to have always applied, to the provisions continued in force by subsection (1).   Endnotes  Endnote 1—Legislation history  Australian Capital Territory Evidence (Temporary Provisions) Act 1971  Endnotes  Endnote 1—Legislation history This endnote sets out details of the legislation history of the Australian Capital Territory Evidence (Temporary Provisions) Act 1971.  Act Number and year Assent Commencement Application, saving and transitional provisions Australian Capital Territory Evidence (Temporary Provisions) Act 1971 66, 1971" ;
    cof:pageNumber "5"^^xsd:integer .

